AB  - This year's results expose a widening gap in students achieving top grades in London and north-east England For international students, 53,740 applicants have been accepted on to undergraduate courses – up by 2% on the 52,640 who were successful last year. Accepted applicants from China rose to 13,870 from 12,380 last year. People have been worried, particularly about what we call the plan two loans, which aren't in place any more. That isn't what people going to university today will be taking on. But, of course, we need to look at ways in which we can make that fairer. Continue reading...
